# EVENTO web — environment template.
# Copy to .env.local for development. Never commit a filled-in copy.
#
# Every value below is server-side only. No provider key may be exposed with a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix: the browser talks only to this app's own /api routes,
# which is also why the Content-Security-Policy can stay at connect-src 'self'.

# Canonical public origin, used for metadata, canonical URLs, robots, the
# sitemap and the AI context surfaces. Production value: https://evento-dev.com
#
# BUILD-TIME value. Those routes are statically generated, so this must be set
# when `npm run build` runs, not only when the server starts. Setting it at
# runtime alone leaves every canonical URL pointing at localhost.
SITE_ORIGIN=

# --- Accounts and project-request storage (optional) ---
# When these are empty the site still renders and the request form degrades to
# an honest "intake not connected" state instead of silently dropping data.
#
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is the anon/publishable key, not a service-role key.
# Authorization is enforced by row level security using each visitor's own
# access token. A service-role key must never be configured for this app.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
